      "fallback_used": false,
      "fallback_reason": null,
      "generated_answer": "Sure — you can switch to a different BS program at LSPU, but there are a few rules you need to follow before doing so.\n\n**Conditions to shift to another BS program**\n\n- **Unit‑failure limit:** You must not fail more than **six (6) units** in any single semester (condition 2.10.1).\n- **Course/major requirements:** You must not fail any course or major‑related subject that appears in the **retention policy** for the target BS’s curriculum (condition 2.10.2).\n- **Shift form:** You need to complete and submit a **filled‑out shifting form** to the **Office of the Registrar** (condition 2.10.3).\n\nIn short, once your enrollment status allows it, you can enroll in any undergraduate BS program, provided you stay within the 6‑unit semester limit, meet all major‑subject retention requirements for that program, and send the official shifting form through the Registrar’s office.",
